---
/**
 * Privacy Policy
 *
 * Written from what this site actually does, not from a template. The site
 * collects almost nothing on its own: there is no account system, no
 * newsletter, and no form anywhere on the site. Everything that follows is
 * checkable against the code — GA4 and a Google Maps embed are the only two
 * third parties that run scripts here, and booking happens on Vagaro, off
 * this domain.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Reveal from '../components/Reveal.astro';
import BreadcrumbSchema from '../components/schema/BreadcrumbSchema.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { business } from '../config/business';

const updated = 'November 7, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | KIAMO Skin"
  description="What KIAMO Skin collects, who it goes to, and how to ask for it to be deleted. Written in plain language, updated November 2026."
>
  <BreadcrumbSchema slot="head" trail={[{ name: 'Privacy Policy', path: '/privacy' }]} />

  <header class="bg-blush">
    <div class="wrap section-y pt-[calc(60px+72px)] md:pt-[calc(60px+112px)]">
      <Breadcrumbs current="Privacy Policy" />
      <h1 class="t-h2 mt-6 max-w-[20ch] text-[2.5rem] md:text-[4rem]">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="t-body mt-7 max-w-[58ch] text-[1.125rem]">
        The short version: this site has no accounts, no newsletter, and no forms. If you
        email or call, what you tell us is used to treat your skin and nothing else.
      </p>
      <p class="t-meta mt-7">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="bg-porcelain">
    <div class="wrap section-y">
      <div class="prose mx-auto max-w-[68ch]">
        <h2 class="t-h3">What we collect when you contact us</h2>
        <p class="t-body mt-5">
          If you call or email the studio, we will ask for your name, a way to reach you back,
          what you want treated, and enough about your skin to plan a protocol — your skin type,
          what you are using, what you have tried, and what has or has not worked. Some of that
          is sensitive health information, and it is treated as such.
        </p>
        <p class="t-body mt-5">
          If you book an appointment, your treatment record, consent notes and aftercare
          instructions are kept in the studio's booking system for as long as the record is
          clinically useful. Clinical records are retained because a treatment plan depends on
          what the skin did last time; that is the whole reason a single practitioner works here
          rather than a rotating team.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-h3 mt-16">What this website collects on its own</h2>
        <p class="t-body mt-5">
          Two things, and only two:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-6 m-0 list-none space-y-4 p-0">
          <li class="t-body flex gap-4">
            <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-rose">—</span>
            <span>
              <strong class="font-medium">Google Analytics.</strong> Page views, where you
              arrived from, and rough device and city information. Google sets cookies for this;
              it is used to see which pages are read, not to build a profile of you. You can
              opt out with the Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li class="t-body flex gap-4">
            <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-rose">—</span>
            <span>
              <strong class="font-medium">A Google Maps embed</strong> on the pages that show
              how to reach the studio. Google may set cookies in that frame.
            </span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="t-body mt-6">
          We set no cookies of our own. There is no tracking pixel, no retargeting, no ad
          platform and no session recording on this site.
        </p>

        <p class="t-body mt-6">
          There is no account to create, no newsletter to subscribe to, and no form on any page
          of this site. The booking form you use lives on Vagaro, a third-party booking system
          that handles your appointment details and your payment. Their privacy policy governs
          what happens there.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-h3 mt-16">Who your information goes to</h2>
        <ul class="mt-6 m-0 list-none space-y-4 p-0">
          <li class="t-body flex gap-4">
            <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-rose">—</span>
            <span>
              <strong class="font-medium">Vagaro</strong>, for appointments and payment. If you
              book, they receive your contact and payment details.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li class="t-body flex gap-4">
            <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-rose">—</span>
            <span>
              <strong class="font-medium">Google</strong>, through Analytics and the Maps embed
              described above.
            </span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="t-body mt-6">
          We do not sell your information, rent it, or share it for anyone else's marketing.
          We do not add you to a mailing list you did not ask for, because there isn't one.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-h3 mt-16">Reviews and photographs</h2>
        <p class="t-body mt-5">
          Client reviews on the <a href="/reviews/">reviews page</a> and the
          <a href="/gallery/">results gallery</a> are published as they were written on the
          studio's Google Business Profile — the same wording, the same reviewer names, the same
          dates. We have not edited them, shortened them, or selected them for tone.
        </p>
        <p class="t-body mt-5">
          Reviewer photographs and profile pictures are reproduced from Google with the review
          they belong to. Before-and-after images of treatment work are published because
          showing the work honestly is the point of the gallery. Your likeness is not used in
          studio marketing without asking first.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-h3 mt-16">How long we keep it</h2>
        <p class="t-body mt-5">
          Clinical records are kept as long as they remain relevant to your skin, and longer
          where the law requires it. Contact records — an email, a voicemail, a booking
          enquiry — are kept for as long as they are useful to you, and no longer.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-h3 mt-16">Your choices</h2>
        <p class="t-body mt-5">
          You can ask what we hold about you, ask for a copy of it, ask for it to be corrected,
          or ask for it to be deleted. Some clinical records have to be kept — a treatment
          record that has been deleted is a treatment record that cannot protect you at the
          next appointment — and where that applies we will tell you plainly rather than
          quietly decline.
        </p>
        <p class="t-body mt-5">
          To ask for anything on this list, email
          <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> or call
          <a href={business.phone.href}>{business.phone.display}</a>. It is a one-room studio
          and a person answers.
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-h3 mt-16">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p class="t-body mt-5">
          If this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it. Nothing on this page is
          a promise about the future; it is a description of what the site does now.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
